) 'Indeed, dear prince, you should know: the celibate life is hard to practice, solitude is difficult to maintain, being alone is hard to enjoy, forest and wilderness retreats are hard to endure, remote lodgings are hard to inhabit, dwelling alone in the forest is painful. For as long as you live, you must dwell among wild beasts; for as long as you live, you must eat food given by others; for as long as you live, you must abstain from human sensual pleasures; for as long as you live, you must abstain from human sports and amusements. Come, dear prince, remain here and exercise the office of crown prince; enjoy sensual pleasures;
give gifts and perform meritorious deeds.' Thus addressed, prince <s>Kāśisundara</s> remained silent.
