  athāyuṣmān mahāmaudgalyāyana āyuṣmantam ānandam idam avocat: yat khalu āyuṣman jānīyaḥ bhagavato mānasam āyuṣmaty ānande pratiṣṭhitam ānando me bhikṣur upasthāsyati manāpena nāmanāpena, bhāṣitaṃ codgrahīṣyati, svaṃ cārthaṃ na riṃciṣyati; tadyathā kūṭāgāre vā kūṭāgāraśālāyāṃ vā uttarāyatāyāṃ prācīnāyatāyāṃ pūrveṇa vātāyanena sūryaraśmayaḥ praviṣya paścimāṃ bhittiṃ niśritya tiṣṭheyuḥ; evam eva bhagavato mānasam āyuṣmaty ānande pratiṣṭhitam ānando me bhikṣur upasthāsyati manāpena nāmanāpena, bhāṣitaṃ codgrahīṣyati, svaṃ cārthaṃ na riṃciṣyati; utsaha tvam āyuṣman ānanda bhagavantam upasthātuṃ, maharddhikā te bhaviṣyati sugataparicaryā; evam aham āyuṣmān mahāmaudgalyāyana utasahe bhagavantam upasthātuṃ sacen me bhagavān trīn varān dadyāt, nāhaṃ bhagavato nirvasanaṃ cīvaraṃ dhārayeyaṃ; nāhaṃ bhagavataḥ paudgalikaṃ nimantraṇaṃ svīkūryāṃ; na ca me kaścid akālaḥ syād bhagavantaṃ darśanāyopasaṃkramituṃ paryupāsanāya; sacen me āyuṣman mahāmaudgalyāyana bhagavān imān trīn varāṃ dadyāt, evam aham utsahe bhagavantam upasthātuṃ, nānyathā.
  athāyuṣmān mahāmaudgalyāyana āyuṣmān śāriputra āyuṣmantam ānandaṃ bhagavata upasthāyakam utsāhya yena bhagavāṃs tenopasaṃkrāntau; upasaṃkramya bhagavataḥ pādau śirasā vanditvaikānte niṣaṇṇau; ekāntaniṣaṇṇo āyuṣmān mahāmaudgalyāyano bhagavantam idam avocat*: utsāhita āvābhyaṃ bhadanta bhikṣur bhagavata upasthāyako yadutāyuṣmān ānanda; sa evam āha: sacen me āyuṣman mahāmaudgalyāyana bhagavāṃs trīn varān dadyād evam aham utsahe bhagavantam upasthātuṃ; nāhaṃ bhagavato nirvasanaṃ cīvaraṃ dhārayeyaṃ, nāhaṃ bhagavataḥ paudgalikaṃ nimantraṇaṃ svīkūryāṃ; na ca me kaścid akālaḥ syād bhagavantaṃ darśanāyopasaṃkramituṃ paryupāsanāya; saced bhagavān imān trīn varān dadyāt, evam aham utsahe bhagavantam upasthātuṃ; sādhu sādhu maudgalyāyana paṇḍita ānando bhikṣuḥ; sa paśyaty anāgataṃ (

body.translated_text:
)
  Then the Venerable <s>Mahāmaudgalyāyana</s> said this to the Venerable <s>Ānanda</s>: 'You should know, Venerable One, that the <s>Bhagavān</s>'s mind is set upon the Venerable <s>Ānanda</s>: "The monk <s>Ānanda</s> will serve me, whether [the conditions are] agreeable or disagreeable; he will retain what is spoken and will not neglect his own spiritual progress." Just as in a gabled hall or a gabled mansion, one long and one facing east, the rays of the sun entering through the eastern window would rest against the western wall — just so, the <s>Bhagavān</s>'s mind is set upon the Venerable <s>Ānanda</s>: "The monk <s>Ānanda</s> will serve me, whether [the conditions are] agreeable or disagreeable; he will retain what is spoken and will not neglect his own spiritual progress." Dare then, Venerable <s>Ānanda</s>, to serve as attendant to the <s>Bhagavān</s>; the service of the <s>Sugata</s> will be of great merit for you.' 'Thus, Venerable <s>Mahāmaudgalyāyana</s>, I dare to serve as attendant to the <s>Bhagavān</s>, provided the <s>Bhagavān</s> grants me three boons: I shall not wear the <s>Bhagavān</s>'s cast-off robes; I shall not accept personal invitations [intended for] the <s>Bhagavān</s>; and there shall be no improper time for me to approach the <s>Bhagavān</s> for an audience and to attend upon him. If, Venerable <s>Mahāmaudgalyāyana</s>, the <s>Bhagavān</s> grants me these three boons, then I dare to serve as attendant to the <s>Bhagavān</s> — not otherwise.'
  Then the Venerable <s>Mahāmaudgalyāyana</s> and the Venerable <s>Śāriputra</s>, having encouraged the Venerable <s>Ānanda</s> to become the <s>Bhagavān</s>'s attendant, approached the <s>Bhagavān</s>. Having approached, they bowed their heads at the <s>Bhagavān</s>'s feet and sat down to one side. Seated to one side, the Venerable <s>Mahāmaudgalyāyana</s> said this to the <s>Bhagavān</s>: 'We two, Venerable Sir, have encouraged a monk to serve as the <s>Bhagavān</s>'s attendant — namely, the Venerable <s>Ānanda</s>. He says thus: "If, Venerable <s>Mahāmaudgalyāyana</s>, the <s>Bhagavān</s> grants me three boons, then I dare to serve as attendant to the <s>Bhagavān</s>: I shall not wear the <s>Bhagavān</s>'s cast-off robes; I shall not accept personal invitations [intended for] the <s>Bhagavān</s>; and there shall be no improper time for me to approach the <s>Bhagavān</s> for an audience and to attend upon him. If the <s>Bhagavān</s> grants these three boons, then I dare to serve as attendant to the <s>Bhagavān</s>." ' 'Excellent, excellent, <s>Maudgalyāyana</s>! The monk <s>Ānanda</s> is wise. He foresees the future (

