  Then <s>Devadatta</s> approached the <s>Bhagavān</s>. Having approached, he bowed his head at the <s>Bhagavān</s>'s feet and stood to one side. Standing to one side, <s>Devadatta</s> said this to the <s>Bhagavān</s>: 'Now the <s>Bhagavān</s> is old, aged, elderly, and is weary of instructing the four assemblies. Would the <s>Bhagavān</s> please hand over the community of monks to me. I shall lead the community of monks. Let the <s>Bhagavān</s> dwell with few concerns, devoted to the practice of pleasant abiding in the present life.' 'I would not hand over the community of monks even to <s>Śāriputra</s> and <s>Maudgalyāyana</s>, those excellent and agreeable fellow practitioners — much less would I hand it over to you, you deluded man, a dead man's spittle!'
  Then <s>Devadatta</s> thought: 'The <s>Bhagavān</s> speaks in praise of <s>Śāriputra</s> and <s>Maudgalyāyana</s>, while he addresses me with the epithet "dead man's spittle."' There <s>Devadatta</s>

