) Whatever pleases and is acceptable to this monk pleases and is acceptable to us as well.'
  The monks reported this matter to the <s>Bhagavān</s>: 'We have admonished <s>Devadatta</s>, Venerable Sir, by the formal act of the fourth motion. When admonished, he stubbornly grasps that very matter, clings to it, and maintains: "This alone is true; anything else is delusion." And his four monk-companions, who are his followers in promoting discord — <s>Kokālika</s>, <s>Khaṇḍadravya</s>, <s>Kaṭamoraka Tiṣya</s>, and <s>Samudradatta</s> — say this to the monks: "Do not, Venerable Ones, say anything to this monk, whether good or bad. For this monk is a speaker of the <s>Dharma</s> and a speaker of the <s>Vinaya</s>. This monk takes up and maintains the <s>Dharma</s> and <s>Vinaya</s>. This monk speaks knowingly, not unknowingly. Whatever pleases and is acceptable to this monk pleases and is acceptable to us as well."'
  The <s>Bhagavān</s> said: 'Monks, admonish <s>Kokālika</s>, <s>Khaṇḍadravya</s>, <s>Kaṭamoraka Tiṣya</s>, and <s>Samudradatta</s> by the friendly admonition. And they should be admonished thus: "Do not you, <s>Kokālika</s>, <s>Khaṇḍadravya</s>, <s>Kaṭamoraka Tiṣya</s>, and <s>Samudradatta</s>, knowingly follow and support in promoting discord one who is a monk exerting himself toward splitting the united <s>Saṅgha</s> and who has taken up and persisted in a dispute that leads to schism. Do not say to the monks: 'Do not, Venerable Ones, say anything to this monk, whether good or bad. For this monk is a speaker of the <s>Dharma</s> and a speaker of the <s>Vinaya</s>. This monk takes up and maintains the <s>Dharma</s> and <s>Vinaya</s>. This monk speaks knowingly, not unknowingly. Whatever pleases and is acceptable to this monk pleases and is acceptable to us as well.' Do not, Venerable Ones, approve of a <s>Saṅgha</s>-schism. Let there be harmony between the Venerable Ones and the <s>Saṅgha</s>. For a <s>Saṅgha</s> that is united, harmonious, rejoicing together, not quarreling, single-minded, with one recitation, blended like milk and water, illuminating the Teacher's teaching, dwells in ease. Let them relinquish

