  Then <s>Devadatta</s> too, with a retinue of five hundred, set out on a tour of the countryside. King <s>Ajātaśatru</s> sent five hundred cartloads of rice covered with leaves along the road for <s>Devadatta</s>. The monks, seeing them, thought: 'Whose are these five hundred cartloads coming?' Being curious, they asked the men on the road, who told them in detail.
  The monks, doubts having arisen, asked the <s>Buddha</s> <s>Bhagavān</s>, who cuts through all doubts: 'See, Venerable Sir — King <s>Ajātaśatru</s> bestows upon the unworthy and rains upon the unworthy.' The <s>Bhagavān</s> said: 'Not only now, monks, does King <s>Ajātaśatru</s> bestow upon the unworthy and rain upon the unworthy; in the past too, he bestowed upon the unworthy and rained upon the unworthy. Listen to this.'

