) 'We must not consume them from this day forward. For what reason? Because of this, calves suffer. The ascetic <s>Gautama</s> consumes meat. We must not consume it. For what reason? Because of this, living beings are killed. The ascetic <s>Gautama</s> consumes salt. We must not consume it — for it is produced from dust. The ascetic <s>Gautama</s> wears robes with cut edges. We must wear robes with long edges. For what reason? Because of this, the labor of weavers is wasted. The ascetic <s>Gautama</s> dwells in the forest. We must dwell in the village. For what reason? Because of this, the charitable gifts of people are not consumed.'
Intervening summary verse (<s>uddāna</s>):
  Milk, meat, and salt; clothing and forest-dwelling. //

