  'How by a formal act of announcement? Just as <s>Devadatta</s> announces, instructs, teaches, and makes the monks understand: "By these five ascetic practices, Venerable ones, a monk is purified, freed, escapes, transcends pleasure and pain, and attains the transcendence of pleasure and pain. Which five? By dwelling in the forest, Venerable ones, a monk is purified, freed, escapes, transcends pleasure and pain, and attains the transcendence of pleasure and pain; by dwelling at tree-roots, by eating only alms-food, by wearing only the triple robe, by wearing only rag-robes, Venerable ones, a monk is purified, freed, escapes, transcends pleasure and pain, and attains the transcendence of pleasure and pain. Whoever among you, Venerable ones, does not approve of being purified, freed, and escaping by these five ascetic practices — let him be far from the ascetic <s>Gautama</s>, let him be distant, let him be far removed!" This is the formal announcement. Thus it is by a formal act of announcement.
